// An error that nothing catches ends the thread it happened on, with a report, and the rest
// of the program goes on.
// expect error output: Uncaught Error: worker gave up

val worker = thread(name = "unlucky") { throw Error("worker gave up") }
worker.join()
print("the thread has ended:", !worker.isAlive)              // expect: the thread has ended: true

// The report says which thread.
// (It reads: Uncaught Error: worker gave up / at <lambda> ... / in thread unlucky)
print("and the program goes on")                             // expect: and the program goes on
